        <body>
            <div xml:id="d871">

                <pb facs="0753" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856B.01/11</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to
                        the British Embassy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi>
                </p>
                <p>In a note dated May 10, 1940 the British Ambassador, acting under instructions
                    from his Government, informed Mr. Hull that His Majesty’s Government in the
                    United Kingdom and the Netherlands Government had agreed that a small British
                    force should be placed at the disposal of the Netherlands authorities in Aruba
                    and Curaçao for the purpose of insuring the security of those islands and of the
                    oil refineries located there.</p>
                <p>Note has been taken of the military dispositions as communicated by Lord Lothian,
                    and the Government of the United States reserves until a later date its comments
                    on the bearing which such dispositions have upon certain long-standing and
                    well-known views and policies of the United States Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-06">July 6,
                            1940</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
